A note on the control flow: `goTo` answers `done` (you are already there / trip landed), `refused` (a real precondition — returned at once, per the task), or `failed` (transient — retried). The loop re-tries only `failed`, doubling the wait each time, up to 6 attempts total; the final `last` is returned regardless of which status it ended on. The `await new Promise(setTimeout…)` yields control back to the runtime rather than busy-looping.

